sequenceDiagram
  title: Command Dispatch (Main Thread) — coconut.call() → WebviewTransport → Lua

  participant JS as JS — coconut.call
  participant SHIM as __coconut_call shim
  participant BIND as __coconut_rpc bind
  participant XPORT as WebviewTransport
  participant REG as commands.Registry
  participant LUA as Lua handler

  JS ->> SHIM : coconut.call("greet", { name:"Ada" })
  SHIM ->> SHIM : build kCall envelope {type,name,payload}
  SHIM ->> BIND : window.__coconut_rpc(msgJson)
  BIND ->> XPORT : static_on_rpc(id, req, arg)

  XPORT ->> XPORT : rpc::Message::fromJson(req[0])
  XPORT ->> XPORT : handleCall(id, msg)
  XPORT ->> REG : handlers.find("greet")

  alt handler registered
    XPORT ->> LUA : fn(paramsTable, ctx) — sol::protected_function — ctx:bind handler
    LUA -->> XPORT : result value or sol::error
    alt result valid
      XPORT ->> XPORT : envelope { ok:true, data:… } — JSON-serialized
    else handler raised
      XPORT ->> XPORT : envelope { ok:false, error:{ code:"LuaError", … } }
    end
  else not registered
    XPORT ->> XPORT : envelope { ok:false, error:{ code:"CommandNotFound", … } }
  end

  XPORT ->> BIND : webview_return(id, 0, envelopeJson)
  BIND -->> SHIM : promise resolves with parsed envelope
  SHIM -->> JS : coconut.call() await returns result / throws

  @start_note right of REG
    ctx:bind()    → handlers    (invoked on main thread in v0.1.1)
    ctx:bind_mt() → mt_handlers (main-thread commands)
    Background-thread execution wiring lands in v0.2.0.
  @end_note